  "question": {
    "text": "The resistance of the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;It is now stretched (keeping the volume constant) without breaking so that its length becomes three times.&nbsp;Now the resistance becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, then what is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1?</mn></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For a given wire, its resistance</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mi>l</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></math></p><p>The wire is stretched such that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>But density is unchanged.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math>Density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mi>V</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>…</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>∵</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∝</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>From <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo>&nbsp;&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>",
